Subject: [PATCH v2] dotfiles/notmuch: Spec reading and sending through
 lab-mail
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: sxmtrkovmkrwqknlsmnsxzumuxuwzzww

Pat reads and sends lab-devel mail from notmuch-emacs on beastie, but
only through the jj maildir. lab-mail now serves the list over IMAP
and relays mail to Fastmail, so the client can use real mail without
holding a credential on beastie. A standalone spec settles the design
before anything is built, as the lab-mail spec did.

Sending as pat@p7x.dev keeps the credential for Pat's primary account
off beastie entirely. A second notmuch profile keeps the jj maildir
intact for the agent's workflow, so Emacs moves to lab-mail with one
setting.

The spec assumes the agent's workflow reads and sends through lab-mail
as well. Once Emacs sends over SMTP, Pat's mail never reaches the jj
maildir, so an agent that reads only the jj maildir would not see it.
